  "name": "Halay (Anatolian davul-zurna line dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Line and circle dance music of central, eastern and southeastern Anatolia, called govend in Kurdish, in which dancers link arms, shoulders or little fingers behind a leader who waves a handkerchief at the head of the line. Davul and zurna play it outdoors at weddings and festivals, and many halays are sung folk songs that open at a moderate tempo and accelerate into a fast closing section; Sivas, Erzincan, Elazığ, Diyarbakır and Gaziantep keep distinct regional halay repertoires.",
  "recipe": "classic modern halay, wedding, middle eastern branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. apricot canonical anatolian ottoman zurna, dance pulse davul. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
